# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF and every working tree gets LF, regardless of the
# platform it is checked out on. Without this, moving the project between
# Windows and Linux made all 25 source files that happened to be checked out
# with CRLF appear rewritten end to end -- 7,646 insertions and 7,646
# deletions whose content was byte-identical. Phantom changes of that size
# hide the real ones, which is the actual cost.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Exceptions, both load-bearing.
#
# gradlew is run by /bin/sh; a CR at the end of its shebang line makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named "sh\r" and the wrapper dies with a
# confusing "bad interpreter" error.
gradlew         text eol=lf
# Batch files are the mirror image: cmd.exe needs CRLF, and gradlew.bat is
# how this project is built on Windows.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Binaries git must never line-ending-convert or try to merge. Listed by what
# this repository actually tracks rather than a generic list: mod and wrapper
# jars, the Vosk grapheme model, store gallery images and the mod icon.
*.jar           binary
*.png           binary
*.bin           binary
*.zip           binary
